[-] Move the canonical RDF projection into Core =core-rdf-projection $Create an always-available clearhead-core rdf module using only lightweight RDF term and serialization dependencies. Move and reconcile graphd's domain-to-RDF and canonical JSON-LD logic so one dataset projection owns all triples, named graphs, stable IRIs, datatypes, deterministic ordering, validation, and every RDF serialization. JSON-LD must serialize the same canonical dataset rather than remain a parallel hand-built graph path. Keep Oxigraph, SPARQL, persistence, networking, and presentation out of Core; prove the normal dependency graph remains database-free.$ !1 ^2026-08-18T21:07 <rdf-dataset-contract #01a01834-581e-70f0-a4c7-0a499ebe4a19
[ ] Expose whole-workspace RDF export from the CLI =cli-rdf-export $Add an always-available clearhead export workspace interface over Core's projection. Support dataset-preserving TriG and N-Quads plus the retained JSON-LD or graph-only formats whose semantics are explicit; cover workspace selection, stdout and output files, empty datasets, deterministic bytes, failures, and broken pipes without duplicating semantic mapping in the CLI.$ !1 ^2026-08-18T21:07 <core-rdf-projection #01a01834-582c-7321-b77c-4986f79793b0
[ ] Make ephemeral local SPARQL an optional CLI capability =optional-sparql $Add a compile-time CLI sparql feature that alone pulls Oxigraph. Load Core's generated ClearHead dataset into an in-memory one-shot store, execute complete raw and saved standard SPARQL, and emit standard SPARQL result or RDF formats. Do not persist state, load arbitrary foreign RDF, federate, proxy endpoints, or reintroduce a ClearHead query language. Define and test minimal and query-enabled build profiles.$ !2 ^2026-08-18T21:07 <core-rdf-projection #01a01834-583a-7b72-ac8e-4ba1f2dfc8e5
[ ] Prove engine-independent RDF publication and queries =external-rdf-proof $Load the CLI's exported dataset into an independent RDF/SPARQL implementation and run the same proving .sparql files unchanged locally and externally. Verify named-graph identity, canonical IDs, representative Charter/Plan/Action/context/dependency facts, ordering fields where contracted, and replace-snapshot behavior. Record exact reproducible commands and any intentionally engine-local behavior.$ !2 ^2026-08-18T21:07 <cli-rdf-export <optional-sparql #01a01834-5848-7de1-a2d0-c88bf0fe45be
[ ] Align documentation, validation, and close the RDF publication charter =close-rdf-publication $Update platform, Core, CLI, ontology, specifications, user docs, dependency gates, and scripts/validate-pinned to describe the final source-of-truth, export, optional-query, and external-database boundaries. Run the complete minimal/full feature matrix and external interoperability proof, record residual risks and promotion triggers for SQL/GQL only if evidence emerged, review the done gate, and close the charter.$ !3 ^2026-08-18T21:07 <retire-graphd #01a01834-5873-76e2-a4fd-b2193e2fcaa7
